WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.670
"We stood by a pond that
winter day," A bare ash tree.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.680
A few fallen leaves.

3
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.010
The sun is white.

4
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.930
The leaves are grey.

5
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.820
Two people stand apart by the water.

6
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.410
Slowly, every colour
drains out of the picture,

7
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.030
until only greys are left.

8
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.040
This is meant to be a love poem.

9
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.830
So why is everything so drained?

10
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.550
In this mission, you'll ask what
a landscape can do in a poem.

11
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.090
Is it just weather?

12
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.310
You'll find out why the last stanza
takes him back to the same place:

13
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.360
"And a pond edged with grayish leaves."

14
00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.230
And you'll ask why Hardy
kept it back so long:

15
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.570
dated 1867, printed in 1898.

16
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.880
Your mission: explain why
this love poem is so drained.
